<title>USA: Exporters sell 162,000 tonnes US corn to unknown.</title>
<headline>Exporters sell 162,000 tonnes US corn to unknown.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Exporters reported the sale of 162,000 tonnes of U.S. corn for delivery to unknown destinations during 1997/98, U.S. Agriculture Department said Friday.</p>
<p>The marketing year will end Aug 30.</p>
<p>By law, exporters must promptly report the sale of 100,000 tonnes or more of a commodity but it sometimes can take a couple of days for the identity of the buyer to become known.</p>
